 "v1_problem": "Billing dispute tickets roughly doubled from ~600/month (Jun-Jul) to 1180-1260/month in Aug-Sep 2026 (E-07/F-06). A field-reader staffing shortfall since July (E-06) is linked to manual-read route completion falling to 0.88 against a 0.95 target across 9,200 accounts (E-01/F-01), which increases estimate-substituted billing and drives part of the surge, but this mechanism explains at most a minority of disputed bills since 59% (1785/3025) were on ACTUAL, not estimated, reads (E-02/F-02/F-03) — leaving a second, not-yet-established mechanism behind most of the surge.",
