 "v2_problem": "Billing dispute tickets rose from ~600/month (Jun-Jul 2026) to 1180-1260/month (Aug-Sep 2026) (E-07) because billing-import validation rule BV-17 -- a high-consumption check with no unit scaling, deployed 2026-08-01 exactly as the surge began (E-12) -- rejects otherwise-valid, timely AMI reads as REJECTED_HIGH_CONSUMPTION and forces estimate substitution, accounting for 1184 of the 1240 ESTIMATED-read disputed bills (95.5%, E-11). Whether this same unscaled rule also drives the larger 59% ACTUAL-read dispute segment remains unconfirmed (H-BV17-UNIT-SCALING-ACTUAL, candidate only).",
 "final_problem": "Billing dispute tickets rose from ~600/month (Jun-Jul 2026) to 1180-1260/month (Aug-Sep 2026) (E-07) because billing-import validation rule BV-17 -- a high-consumption check with no unit scaling, deployed 2026-08-01 exactly as the surge began (E-12) -- rejects otherwise-valid, timely AMI reads as REJECTED_HIGH_CONSUMPTION and forces estimate substitution, accounting for 1184 of the 1240 ESTIMATED-read disputed bills (95.5%, E-11). Whether this same unscaled rule also drives the larger 59% ACTUAL-read dispute segment remains unconfirmed (H-BV17-UNIT-SCALING-ACTUAL, candidate only).",
